<<<
2. Absolute construction. The Municipal Council, having refused their assistant clerks’ demand for a rise in salary, those in the Food Supply offices today declared a strike.
===
**2. Absolute construction.** *The Municipal Council, having refused their assistant clerks’ demand for a rise in salary, those in the Food Supply offices today declared a strike.*
>>>

<<<
no comma after Council) is an example of what is perhaps both the worst & the commonest of all mistakes in punctuation, See ABSO- LUTE CONSTRUCTION.
===
no comma after *Council*) is an example of what is perhaps both the worst & the commonest of all mistakes in punctuation. See ^^ABSOLUTE CONSTRUCTION^^.
>>>

